ion FD disclosure","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465926012164/0001104659-26-012164-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-01-29","form":"8-K","codes":["1.01"],"events":[{"label":"Material agreement entered","kind":"deal","tone":"good"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465926007556/0001104659-26-007556-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-12-17","form":"8-K","codes":["1.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Material agreement entered","kind":"deal","tone":"good"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465925122063/0001104659-25-122063-index.htm"},{"date":"2025-12-02","form":"8-K","codes":["5.02","7.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Director or officer departure or appointment","kind":"people","tone":"warn"},{"label":"Regulation FD disclosure","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465925117801/0001104659-25-117801-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[{"date":"2024-08-07","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000093041324002266/0000930413-24-002266-index.htm","tone":"warn"}],"summary":{"sentences":["Seaport Entertainment Group Inc. files with the SEC under \"Services-Miscellaneous Amusement & Recreation\", based in NY, and has been publicly reporting for 1 year.","It reported $113.7m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, down 20.7% against the same quarter a year earlier.","Listed on NYSE, it is still consuming cash, with roughly 28 months of runway at the current burn."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Net cash of $76.5m against total assets of $541.8m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465926056380/0001104659-26-056380-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-056380"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.2% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465926056380/0001104659-26-056380-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-056380"}],"bear":[{"text":"Revenue fell 20.7% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). Whatever the story is, it is not currently showing up in sales.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465926056380/0001104659-26-056380-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-056380"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-333.8% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465926056380/0001104659-26-056380-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-056380"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $9.8m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465926056380/0001104659-26-056380-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-056380"},{"text":"About 28 months of cash at the current burn ($114.8m against $49.6m a year). A company that must raise is a company that raises on the buyer's terms.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000110465926056380/0001104659-26-056380-index.htm","accession":"0001104659-26-056380"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 1.4% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2009684/000184855426000004/0001848554-26-000004-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below -36.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":-0.36,"consecutive":2,"current":-0.207,"current_display":"-20.7%","threshold_display":"-36.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":27.769,"current_display":"28 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"rationale":"Below twelve months the company raises on whatever terms it can get, and that dilution lands on you.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":0.002,"current_display":"0.2%","threshold_display":"10.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.00","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"above","threshold":1.0,"consecutive":1,"current":0.093,"current_display":"0.09","threshold_display":"1.00","fired":false,"rationale":"Past this point creditors, not shareholders, decide what happens next.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears in any filing","metric":"going_concern","comparison":"is_true","threshold":true,"current":false,"current_display":"not present","fired":false,"rationale":"The auditors saying the company may not survive the year is not a signal to interpret. It is the exit.","editable":false}],"team":[{"raw_name":"Matthew Morris Partridge","role":"Officer","title_filed":"Chief Executiv